  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "First of all thanks for the avatar scale slider that was implemented with the new patch.\n\nI would like to add a suggestion for the scale slider:\n\nAn Avatar Height upper bound setting.\n\nIt would be nice to have an option to define the upper limit of the scale slider, allowing values from 1-5m.\n\nThis way small avatar users can get more out of the scale slider and better fine tune there size. Because with the current implementation they will only use the lower 10% of the slider.\n\nIf your default avatar height is 0.7m its very difficult to fine tune anyting around the snapping point.\n\nAnother solution would be a scale, where your default size (as defined in unity) is at 50% of the slider (the snapping point)",
